# Licensing

This repository uses three licenses, applied by directory. Each directory's
contents are covered by exactly one of them.

## docs/ and spec/ — CC-BY-4.0

The non-normative documentation under `docs/` and the normative specification
under `spec/` are licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
International license. Full text in [`LICENSE-CC-BY`](LICENSE-CC-BY).

You are free to share, adapt, and quote these materials in academic papers,
other specifications, and derivative documents, provided attribution is
preserved.

## implementations/python/ — Apache-2.0

The Python reference implementation under `implementations/python/` is
licensed under the Apache License 2.0. Full text in
[`LICENSE-APACHE`](LICENSE-APACHE).

The Apache 2.0 patent grant is intentional: it gives downstream commercial
implementers more comfort than a permissive license without an explicit
patent grant.

## test-vectors/ — CC0 1.0

The cross-implementation test vectors under `test-vectors/` are released into
the public domain under the Creative Commons CC0 1.0 Universal dedication.
Full text in [`LICENSE-CC0`](LICENSE-CC0).

This is intentional: test fixtures should have zero attribution burden so
that any implementation in any language can ship them as part of its own
test suite without dragging in license obligations.

## Other directories

`README.md`, `CHANGELOG.md`, `CONTRIBUTING.md`, and other top-level metadata
files are CC-BY-4.0, same as `docs/`.

The C# implementation under `implementations/csharp/`, when it lands, will
declare its own license inside that directory. The expected license is
Apache-2.0, matching the Python reference implementation, but this is the
C# implementer's call.
